NUM-45: set the concentration of a dry node with no inflow to zero

The non-storage branch of QualitySolver::mixAtNodes() published a dry node's
summed load rate (qual_mass_in, mass/s) as its concentration when the node
had no inflow, copying 5.3.0. A node with no water has no concentration:
report 0, as 5.2.4 does. Wet nodes and nodes with inflow are unchanged.

test_quality_routing's ResidualInflowBelowLegacyZeroIsNotDividedBy expected
the 5.3.0 load-rate residue (1e-14 x 1e5) at its dry node; it now expects 0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-45_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/quality/QualityRouting.cpp b/src/engine/quality/QualityRouting.cpp
index 917fc1d..b5a5c29 100644
--- a/src/engine/quality/QualityRouting.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/quality/QualityRouting.cpp
@@ -1111,14 +1111,10 @@ void QualitySolver::mixAtNodes(SimulationContext& ctx, double dt) {
                     // quality.
                     nodes.conc[idx] = nodes.conc_old[idx];
                 } else {
-                    // A DRY one leaves Node.newQual as the accumulator
-                    // (qualrout.c findNodeQual): the summed q*c load rate,
-                    // published as its concentration. The inflow is only
-                    // at or below ZERO (1e-10 cfs), not absent, so the
-                    // load is tiny but not zero (1943-h-h-elements-si-units
-                    // reports 1e-10..1e-13 mg/L there).
-                    nodes.conc[idx] = (idx < nodes.qual_mass_in.size())
-                                    ? nodes.qual_mass_in[idx] : 0.0;
+                    // A DRY one holds no water, so no concentration
+                    // (5.2.4 findNodeQual). Its summed load rate
+                    // (qual_mass_in) is not a concentration.
+                    nodes.conc[idx] = 0.0;
                 }
             }
             continue;
